      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 56‑mile railroad, completed just 157 days after the San Joaquin & Eastern Railroad Company was organized, was an engineering feat for the remote area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bigcreekgeneralstore.com/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original penstock pipes for Big Creek Power Houses One and Two were German Krupp steel, chosen for their high tensile strength to handle a 1,500‑foot drop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Creek%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s only way in or out is Big Creek Road off State Route 168, a reminder of its isolated origins.",
